- Furnace. - with other households.

1307
00:52:01,431 --> 00:52:02,831
There were many such townhouses in the past.

1308
00:52:04,971 --> 00:52:06,871
A piano academy was here.

1309
00:52:09,101 --> 00:52:10,141
I could remember it.

1310
00:52:10,141 --> 00:52:11,841
I could remember that part of the neighborhood.

1311
00:52:12,211 --> 00:52:14,011
A piano academy. An art academy.

1312
00:52:14,681 --> 00:52:15,681
That's right.

1313
00:52:15,681 --> 00:52:17,581
(Everything changed.)

1314
00:52:19,111 --> 00:52:20,821
Five to six years ago,

1315
00:52:20,821 --> 00:52:22,621
- such traces remained. - I see.

1316
00:52:22,991 --> 00:52:24,091
It disappointed me.

1317
00:52:24,121 --> 00:52:25,521
Had you come sooner...

1318
00:52:27,891 --> 00:52:29,661
I should call my mom.

1319
00:52:33,501 --> 00:52:34,901
- Hello? - Mom.

1320
00:52:35,101 --> 00:52:36,731
- Yes? - Do you know where I'm at?

1321
00:52:36,731 --> 00:52:38,371
- Y Townhouse... - Okay.

1322
00:52:38,371 --> 00:52:40,741
and the public housing apartments are completely gone.

1323
00:52:40,801 --> 00:52:42,971
Oh, my gosh. Are there new apartments?

1324
00:52:42,971 --> 00:52:44,611
It's full of new apartments.

1325
00:52:44,611 --> 00:52:47,341
- I see. The memories are gone. - Everything is gone.

1326
00:52:47,341 --> 00:52:50,081
You know my friends from Gwansan Elementary School...

1327
00:52:50,081 --> 00:52:52,951
such as Jong Bae and Won Seok. Do they still live here?

1328
00:52:53,151 --> 00:52:54,581
- Of course. - What?

1329
00:52:54,581 --> 00:52:57,721
Does Won Seok's mom still run a restaurant?

1330
00:52:57,721 --> 00:52:58,721
Yes, she does.

1331
00:52:58,721 --> 00:53:00,391
I thought it'd be nice to visit her.

1332
00:53:00,391 --> 00:53:01,891
She'll be thankful.

1333
00:53:01,891 --> 00:53:03,861
- Okay. - All right.

1334
00:53:04,791 --> 00:53:07,261
Since I called my mom, I should visit her.

1335
00:53:09,471 --> 00:53:11,331
Does your friend's mom still run...

1336
00:53:11,331 --> 00:53:13,001
- a restaurant there? - Yes, she does.

1337
00:53:13,001 --> 00:53:14,471
- It's here. - You should visit right away.

1338
00:53:17,811 --> 00:53:19,041
Would she recognize me?

1339
00:53:19,041 --> 00:53:20,211
(Would she remember my face?)

1340
00:53:21,541 --> 00:53:22,811
It was nerve-racking...

1341
00:53:22,811 --> 00:53:23,911
- since it had been a while. - Of course.

1342
00:53:23,911 --> 00:53:25,111
- That's right. - Of course, it was nerve-racking.

1343
00:53:25,551 --> 00:53:28,181
- Of course, it was nerve-racking. - "Would she remember me?"

1344
00:53:28,321 --> 00:53:30,491
I feel like I'm watching "TV Loaded with Love."

1345
00:53:38,361 --> 00:53:39,391
Ma'am.

1346
00:53:39,391 --> 00:53:43,131
- Oh, my! Look at you! - My goodness.

1347
00:53:43,131 --> 00:53:45,201
- Oh, my! - She recognized him right away.

1348
00:53:46,441 --> 00:53:48,641
She threw her kitchen towel.

1349
00:53:48,641 --> 00:53:50,211
My goodness.

1350
00:53:50,541 --> 00:53:52,471
Look at you!

1351
00:53:52,471 --> 00:53:53,841
(I'm here, ma'am.)

1352
00:53:53,841 --> 00:53:55,511
I didn't expect to see a star here.

1353
00:53:55,711 --> 00:53:58,081
It's an honor to my family.

1354
00:53:58,081 --> 00:54:00,581
- It's so good to see you again. - You're handsome.

1355
00:54:00,581 --> 00:54:01,781
(He quietly hugs her again.)

1356
00:54:02,381 --> 00:54:04,151
(She's the mom of Dae Ho's friend, Won Seok.)

1357
00:54:04,351 --> 00:54:06,461
The visit was so belated. I didn't even call her beforehand.

1358
00:54:06,761 --> 00:54:08,791
- Hello. Gosh, Hyeon Seok. - This is Hyeon Seok's mom.

1359
00:54:09,561 --> 00:54:11,261
(And there's Hyeon Seok's mom as well.)

1360
00:54:11,861 --> 00:54:14,061
(Ahn Eun Yeong, Hyeon Seok's mom)

1361
00:54:14,061 --> 00:54:15,201
My goodness.

1362
00:54:15,201 --> 00:54:16,431
I didn't expect to see a star here.

1363
00:54:16,431 --> 00:54:18,671
- You're too kind. - Dae Ho.

1364
00:54:18,701 --> 00:54:19,941
I was...

1365
00:54:20,371 --> 00:54:22,301
Are you crying because you're so happy to see us?

1366
00:54:22,641 --> 00:54:24,671
- My goodness. - What brings you here?

1367
00:54:24,741 --> 00:54:26,071
I wasn't going to cry.

1368
00:54:26,741 --> 00:54:28,211
- Oh, no. - This brings back memories.

1369
00:54:28,211 --> 00:54:29,811
Why are you crying?

1370
00:54:29,811 --> 00:54:31,251
- Why are you crying? - My goodness.

1371
00:54:31,251 --> 00:54:32,351
Gosh.

1372
00:54:33,451 --> 00:54:34,821
I wasn't going to cry.

1373
00:54:35,281 --> 00:54:36,951
- I'm becoming teary-eyed too. - This brings back memories.

1374
00:54:36,951 --> 00:54:37,951
- This brings back memories. - Yes.

1375
00:54:37,951 --> 00:54:39,021
You remember, right?

1376
00:54:39,021 --> 00:54:41,391
- Of course. - We were young.

1377
00:54:41,391 --> 00:54:43,091
It was so touching.

1378
00:54:43,331 --> 00:54:46,531
I felt like I had gone back to my young self.

1379
00:54:46,631 --> 00:54:48,861
My friends' moms seemed so big back then.

1380
00:54:49,501 --> 00:54:50,771
But they looked so small now.

1381
00:54:50,771 --> 00:54:53,241
- I think I get it. - It made me feel...

1382
00:54:53,341 --> 00:54:55,701
many emotions.

1383
00:54:56,001 --> 00:54:58,311
It stimulated my lachrymal glands.

1384
00:54:58,311 --> 00:54:59,581
(I ended up crying again.)

1385
00:54:59,581 --> 00:55:01,381
- That's right. - I shed tears again.

1386
00:55:01,941 --> 00:55:03,911
- It's so nice... - Please take a seat.

1387
00:55:03,911 --> 00:55:05,281
to see you.

1388
00:55:05,281 --> 00:55:06,421
- Fruits. - I...

1389
00:55:06,681 --> 00:55:07,951
(You shouldn't have!)

1390
00:55:07,951 --> 00:55:09,481
- It's like a box of fruits. - It would've been nice...

1391
00:55:09,481 --> 00:55:12,051
to stay longer for a meal.

1392
00:55:12,051 --> 00:55:14,461
- But I only have a moment. - Although it's sudden,

1393
00:55:14,461 --> 00:55:16,191
it's so good to see you again.

1394
00:55:16,191 --> 00:55:18,191
- Ma'am, please have some fruit. - Seriously.

1395
00:55:18,191 --> 00:55:20,001
All right. You should eat.

1396
00:55:20,301 --> 00:55:21,861
Dae Ho, you should eat.

1397
00:55:22,001 --> 00:55:24,101
You still have the looks from childhood.

1398
00:55:24,101 --> 00:55:25,601
- Do you remember me from back then? - Yes.

1399
00:55:25,601 --> 00:55:26,701
- Do you remember me as a child? - Of course.

1400
00:55:27,071 --> 00:55:29,301
Even as a child, you were mature.

1401
00:55:29,711 --> 00:55:31,911
When I was young,

1402
00:55:32,011 --> 00:55:34,081
- I didn't play energetically. - That's right.

1403
00:55:34,081 --> 00:55:35,611
- You were mature. - Yes.

1404
00:55:35,611 --> 00:55:38,681
You were thoughtful and well-mannered.

1405
00:55:38,681 --> 00:55:39,781
- Ma'am, please take a seat. - Seriously.

1406
00:55:39,921 --> 00:55:42,851
Seriously, you were thoughtful.

1407
00:55:43,221 --> 00:55:46,661
- You were like an adult. - That's right.

1408
00:55:47,191 --> 00:55:49,491
I think she welcomes him more than her own son.

1409
00:55:50,491 --> 00:55:52,561
- He returned home in glory. - That's right.

1410
00:55:52,761 --> 00:55:55,001
Are Won Seok and the others doing well?

1411
00:55:55,001 --> 00:55:56,371
- Yes. They're doing well. - I see.

1412
00:55:56,471 --> 00:55:58,001
Won Seok has two children.

1413
00:55:58,001 --> 00:55:59,371
- Gosh. - Tae Ho...

1414
00:56:00,241 --> 00:56:01,341
has one daughter.

1415
00:56:02,041 --> 00:56:03,171
- Everyone is married. - Yes.

1416
00:56:03,841 --> 00:56:04,971
What does Min Ji do?

1417
00:56:05,511 --> 00:56:06,911
(Who's that?)

1418
00:56:06,981 --> 00:56:08,441
She became a flight attendant for Korean Air.

1419
00:56:08,541 --> 00:56:09,751
Really?

1420
00:56:09,751 --> 00:56:12,851
(Min Ji became a flight attendant.)

1421
00:56:12,851 --> 00:56:14,051
- Why are you so happy? - He looks so happy.

1422
00:56:14,051 --> 00:56:15,281
- A flight attendant? - Yes.

1423
00:56:15,551 --> 00:56:17,821
I have a friend named Won Seok.

1424
00:56:18,151 --> 00:56:20,191
He has a younger sister named Ko Min Ji.

1425
00:56:20,191 --> 00:56:21,991
- I see. - Yes. She was very pretty.

1426
00:56:21,991 --> 00:56:23,991
So you had an ulterior motive.

1427
00:56:23,991 --> 00:56:25,891
- An ulterior motive? - That was why you went there.

1428
00:56:25,891 --> 00:56:26,961
Come on.

1429
00:56:26,961 --> 00:56:28,531
- What was your goal? - That was why you went there.

1430
00:56:28,631 --> 00:56:30,371
- I mean... - You had an ulterior motive.

1431
00:56:30,531 --> 00:56:32,001
She must be around the age...

1432
00:56:32,001 --> 00:56:33,701
- to get married. - That's right.

1433
00:56:34,271 --> 00:56:35,701
He went there wearing Joo Woo Jae's shirt.

1434
00:56:35,701 --> 00:56:37,111
- He had an impure goal. - A friend's younger sister.

1435
00:56:37,311 --> 00:56:39,271
(A style that makes him the parents' favorite)

1436
00:56:39,271 --> 00:56:40,981
She has worked for 14 years.

1437
00:56:42,041 --> 00:56:43,181
She's like me.

1438
00:56:43,451 --> 00:56:45,011
- Min Ji... - Min Ji got married as well.

1439
00:56:45,011 --> 00:56:46,751
(Min Ji got married as well.)

1440
00:56:46,751 --> 00:56:48,381
- Did she get married? - She has one daughter.

1441
00:56:48,481 --> 00:56:49,551
Of course, she got married.

1442
00:56:49,551 --> 00:56:50,871
(His eyes lose their shine.)

1443
00:56:50,918 --> 00:56:52,088
- Min Ji... - Min Ji got married as well.

1444
00:56:52,088 --> 00:56:53,288
- Did she get married? - She has one daughter.

1445
00:56:53,288 --> 00:56:54,428
Of course, she got married.

1446
00:56:54,428 --> 00:56:55,728
- Min Ji got married as well. - Min Ji...

1447
00:56:55,988 --> 00:56:57,128
(Did she get married?)

1448
00:56:57,128 --> 00:56:59,598
- His tears stopped. - My tears stopped.

1449
00:56:59,968 --> 00:57:01,128
She's a parent now.

1450
00:57:02,468 --> 00:57:04,398
- Min Ji was pretty back in the day. - She was pretty.

1451
00:57:05,438 --> 00:57:06,938
(Just eat more fruit.)

1452
00:57:06,938 --> 00:57:08,038
"Just eat more fruit."

1453
00:57:08,368 --> 00:57:09,708
He came too late.

1454
00:57:10,108 --> 00:57:11,508
(He soothes the heartbreak with fruit.)

1455
00:57:11,508 --> 00:57:12,538
You know,

1456
00:57:13,148 --> 00:57:14,308
at first,

1457
00:57:15,508 --> 00:57:16,778
I felt a bit awkward...

1458
00:57:16,778 --> 00:57:19,048
- because I hadn't called before. - Right.

1459
00:57:19,748 --> 00:57:21,048
But seeing you made me so happy.

1460
00:57:21,048 --> 00:57:24,618
We didn't meet as adults.

1461
00:57:24,758 --> 00:57:26,018
We've known each other...

1462
00:57:26,018 --> 00:57:27,288
- since your elementary school days. - That's right.

1463
00:57:27,288 --> 00:57:29,458
- That's why... - My goodness.

1464
00:57:29,458 --> 00:57:31,028
- it's like that. - You brought paper.

1465
00:57:31,028 --> 00:57:32,228
- We have a history. - I want your autograph.

1466
00:57:32,228 --> 00:57:33,528
- Autograph. - She wants his autograph.

1467
00:57:33,528 --> 00:57:35,028
- We have a history. - He should give his autograph.

1468
00:57:35,398 --> 00:57:36,868
- You must be hungry. - Okay.

1469
00:57:36,868 --> 00:57:38,968
(I need Dae Ho's autograph.)

1470
00:57:38,968 --> 00:57:40,208
(Laughing)

1471
00:57:41,708 --> 00:57:43,278
"Stop talking and sign here."

1472
00:57:43,278 --> 00:57:44,478
(I can give you as much fruit as you want.)

1473
00:57:45,578 --> 00:57:46,978
You know, my mom...

1474
00:57:48,048 --> 00:57:49,278
moved to Yangpyeong...

1475
00:57:49,278 --> 00:57:50,778
(Eating)

1476
00:57:51,048 --> 00:57:52,048
You must be hungry.
(Kind)

1477
00:57:53,288 --> 00:57:55,388
My mom moved to Yangpyeong and felt very lonely.

1478
00:57:55,618 --> 00:57:57,188
But talking with you guys on the phone...

1479
00:57:57,188 --> 00:57:58,758
gave her strength.

1480
00:57:58,758 --> 00:58:00,828
She talked about you guys a lot.

1481
00:58:01,258 --> 00:58:03,228
- We had a lot of fun back then. - That's right.

1482
00:58:03,328 --> 00:58:05,158
The Moms' Association members remained close.

1483
00:58:05,158 --> 00:58:07,368
- Moms were young back then. - Children rarely met up.

1484
00:58:07,428 --> 00:58:08,498
That's right.

1485
00:58:08,498 --> 00:58:10,138
- But the parents remained close. - The parents.

1486
00:58:10,638 --> 00:58:12,538
In the beginning, you guys formed a group...

1487
00:58:12,538 --> 00:58:14,338
- for the children's sake. - That's right.

1488
00:58:14,338 --> 00:58:15,868
When I look back on it now,

1489
00:58:16,308 --> 00:58:18,408
I feel so thankful for the parents.

1490
00:58:18,638 --> 00:58:20,448
I didn't have many friends...

1491
00:58:20,448 --> 00:58:21,908
- back in elementary school. - That's right.

1492
00:58:21,908 --> 00:58:24,278
- That's right. - After the field day,

1493
00:58:24,278 --> 00:58:26,348
- we ate together. - That's right. We did that.

1494
00:58:26,348 --> 00:58:27,748
We gathered around and ate together.

1495
00:58:28,688 --> 00:58:30,688
(They did everything together like a family in his childhood.)

1496
00:58:30,688 --> 00:58:32,488
- It's an old clip. - That's from my childhood.

1497
00:58:32,688 --> 00:58:34,728
- There were flags of all nations. - That's right.

1498
00:58:34,728 --> 00:58:36,958
These days, elementary schoolers don't eat like that.

1499
00:58:37,228 --> 00:58:38,428
That culture disappeared.

1500
00:58:39,128 --> 00:58:41,798
We were very happy when you guys were in elementary school.

1501
00:58:41,798 --> 00:58:43,268
Every weekend,

1502
00:58:43,268 --> 00:58:45,838
moms and dads played soccer in the park...

1503
00:58:45,838 --> 00:58:47,138
and grilled meat.

1504
00:58:47,138 --> 00:58:48,268
I remember that.

1505
00:58:48,838 --> 00:58:49,908
- Yes. - It was fun.

1506
00:58:50,538 --> 00:58:52,478
We even visited your mom in Yangpyeong.

1507
00:58:52,478 --> 00:58:53,508
We did that often.

1508
00:58:53,508 --> 00:58:54,708
- That's right. - At the house...

1509
00:58:54,708 --> 00:58:56,978
- You guys met up recently. - Yes.

1510
00:58:56,978 --> 00:58:57,978
That's right.

1511
00:58:57,978 --> 00:58:59,888
That's why we're so happy to see you here.

1512
00:58:59,888 --> 00:59:02,018
The two of you haven't changed at all.

1513
00:59:02,018 --> 00:59:04,018
(The two of you haven't changed at all.)

1514
00:59:04,018 --> 00:59:05,088
- No way. - We became old.

1515
00:59:05,088 --> 00:59:07,628
- No. You guys look the same. - Time has changed us.

1516
00:59:08,028 --> 00:59:09,528
- You guys look the same. - My goodness.

1517
00:59:09,858 --> 00:59:11,498
- It's so good to see you. - It's so good to see you.

1518
00:59:11,498 --> 00:59:13,868
You guys seemed so tall back then.

1519
00:59:13,868 --> 00:59:14,928
That's right.

1520
00:59:14,928 --> 00:59:16,538
- You guys were young back then. - That's right.

1521
00:59:16,538 --> 00:59:17,998
- Our heights are matched now. - Yes.

1522
00:59:17,998 --> 00:59:19,498
- He's crying again. - We became shorter.

1523
00:59:19,498 --> 00:59:21,238
Having good memories makes you cry more.

1524
00:59:21,238 --> 00:59:22,238
Still, you guys are healthy.

1525
00:59:22,238 --> 00:59:23,938
- Both of them look young. - That's right.

1526
00:59:23,938 --> 00:59:25,938
That was why I was even more surprised.

1527
00:59:26,038 --> 00:59:27,278
It must feel so strange for them.

1528
00:59:27,278 --> 00:59:29,178
- You were in elementary school. - I know.

1529
00:59:29,178 --> 00:59:30,478
- But you became this way. - It must be shocking.

1530
00:59:30,478 --> 00:59:31,778
- Seriously. - "You became this way?"

1531
00:59:32,218 --> 00:59:34,488
I didn't mean it like that.

1532
00:59:34,918 --> 00:59:36,248
It's a class reunion, right?

1533
00:59:36,248 --> 00:59:37,388
- Seriously. - A class reunion.

1534
00:59:37,388 --> 00:59:39,058
- A class reunion! - I didn't know that.

1535
00:59:39,058 --> 00:59:40,588
- They're 2 years older. - They're 2 years older.

1536
00:59:40,788 --> 00:59:42,658
I'll keep crying if I stay here.

1537
00:59:42,658 --> 00:59:43,858
I was only visiting for a short while.

1538
00:59:43,858 --> 00:59:46,098
- I'll keep in touch through Mom. - Okay.

1539
00:59:46,328 --> 00:59:49,228
It would've been nice to eat with you if you weren't busy.

1540
00:59:50,138 --> 00:59:51,598
I can't believe Min Ji got married.

1541
00:59:52,868 --> 00:59:54,538
They will think that you're drunk.

1542
00:59:54,708 --> 00:59:56,038
- That's barley tea. - When you're at the airport,

1543
00:59:56,778 --> 00:59:59,778
see if the name on the name tag says, "Ko Min Ji."

1544
01:00:00,278 --> 01:00:02,078
- Then... - Does she still go on flights?

1545
01:00:02,078 --> 01:00:03,318
- Of course. - I see.

1546
01:00:03,318 --> 01:00:04,318
That's right.

1547
01:00:04,348 --> 01:00:06,918
Then she must know many junior flight attendants.

1548
01:00:06,918 --> 01:00:07,948
Of course.

1549
01:00:07,948 --> 01:00:08,948
(Smiling after sniffling)

1550
01:00:09,618 --> 01:00:10,658
(He laughs after crying.)

1551
01:00:10,658 --> 01:00:11,658
That's right.

1552
01:00:11,658 --> 01:00:13,728
You did a good job of making it sound like a joke.

1553
01:00:15,488 --> 01:00:17,598
I have an appointment.

1554
01:00:17,758 --> 01:00:19,828
Although it hasn't been long, I must get going now.

1555
01:00:19,828 --> 01:00:22,068
Then eat this before you go. You don't want to get thirsty.

1556
01:00:22,668 --> 01:00:24,438
Have a sip of pu'er tea before you go.

1557
01:00:24,838 --> 01:00:26,368
- Thank you. - Ma'am, please stay healthy.

1558
01:00:26,368 --> 01:00:28,738
Thank you so much for visiting.

1559
01:00:28,738 --> 01:00:29,938
- I'll keep in touch. - Okay.

1560
01:00:29,938 --> 01:00:31,708
- Bye. - We'll see each other again.

1561
01:00:31,708 --> 01:00:33,278
- All right. Let's meet again. - Bye, Dae Ho.

1562
01:00:33,278 --> 01:00:34,578
- I'll get going. - Okay.

1563
01:00:35,078 --> 01:00:36,748
You should go back inside. You don't need to see me off.

1564
01:00:36,748 --> 01:00:37,748
My goodness.

1565
01:00:38,548 --> 01:00:40,548
(You don't need to see me off.)

1566
01:00:40,548 --> 01:00:42,448
He's my son.

1567
01:00:42,588 --> 01:00:43,788
- Hello. - He's handsome, right?

1568
01:00:43,918 --> 01:00:46,088
It was so nice to hear her call me her son.

1569
01:00:46,088 --> 01:00:47,388
- Hello. - Kim Dae Ho.

1570
01:00:48,528 --> 01:00:50,358
Please go back inside. I'll keep in touch.

1571
01:00:54,828 --> 01:00:56,838
It'll be funny if he suddenly goes to the airport.

1572
01:00:57,468 --> 01:00:58,938
"Ma'am, I'm at the Incheon..."

1573
01:00:58,938 --> 01:01:00,368
- "International Airport." - I'm not at the airport.

1574
01:01:00,638 --> 01:01:02,268
- I'm not at the airport. - You're at the airport.

1575
01:01:02,268 --> 01:01:03,408
- He'll go, - "I'm here."

1576
01:01:03,408 --> 01:01:04,878
"Where's Ko Min Ji?"

1577
01:01:04,878 --> 01:01:07,248
"I just ended up coming here."

1578
01:01:09,078 --> 01:01:10,148
(Dae Ho arrives at a place.)

1579
01:01:10,148 --> 01:01:11,148
Look at his eyes.

1580
01:01:11,148 --> 01:01:12,878
"Where's the counter for Korean Air?"

1581
01:01:13,988 --> 01:01:16,118
I wouldn't know where to go without an address.

1582
01:01:16,518 --> 01:01:18,788
After attending Gwansan Elementary School,

1583
01:01:18,788 --> 01:01:20,988
I briefly attended Sigok Elementary School.

1584
01:01:21,428 --> 01:01:22,758
You moved around a lot.

1585
01:01:23,328 --> 01:01:24,998
This didn't exist when I lived here.

1586
01:01:27,528 --> 01:01:29,368
I should take this route. After going this way...

1587
01:01:30,338 --> 01:01:31,468
It's over there.

1588
01:01:34,208 --> 01:01:35,638
This place is very meaningful.

1589
01:01:35,908 --> 01:01:37,208
Mom applied for an apartment and got it...

1590
01:01:37,208 --> 01:01:38,608
through a housing subscription savings account.

1591
01:01:39,378 --> 01:01:42,148
Back then, my dad made 240 dollars a month.

1592
01:01:42,748 --> 01:01:46,218
But 100 dollars a month went into the deposit.

1593
01:01:47,418 --> 01:01:49,648
Back then, everyone struggled financially.

1594
01:01:50,258 --> 01:01:52,388
My parents started with nothing.

1595
01:01:53,158 --> 01:01:55,188
But... An apartment?

1596
01:01:55,528 --> 01:01:57,928
- It was the symbol of success. - It was everyone's dream.

1597
01:01:58,058 --> 01:02:01,228
The young couple was so excited about getting an apartment.

1598
01:02:01,898 --> 01:02:06,098
Back then, only the living room had linoleum flooring.

1599
01:02:06,608 --> 01:02:08,068
There were three rooms.

1600
01:02:08,268 --> 01:02:09,908
One master bedroom and two small rooms.

1601
01:02:10,338 --> 01:02:12,378
To save up money,

1602
01:02:13,248 --> 01:02:15,578
Mom and Dad bought varnish and applied it on the floor.

1603
01:02:15,578 --> 01:02:17,148
That was how much they cherished the apartment.

1604
01:02:17,148 --> 01:02:20,488
I followed my dad around when he did that.

1605
01:02:20,988 --> 01:02:24,318
While we waited for the varnish to dry,

1606
01:02:24,318 --> 01:02:26,018
- we ate jjajangmyeon. - We ate jjajangmyeon that day.

1607
01:02:26,488 --> 01:02:27,488
It must've been tasty.

1608
01:02:27,758 --> 01:02:29,898
We visited the apartment all the time...

1609
01:02:29,898 --> 01:02:31,498
- even before moving in. - You guys were so happy.

1610
01:02:31,928 --> 01:02:34,628
The neighborhood has that apartment...

1611
01:02:35,028 --> 01:02:37,068
as well as the school I attended.

1612
01:02:37,368 --> 01:02:38,498
That was why I visited the neighborhood.

1613
01:02:38,938 --> 01:02:40,668
(Ansan, Gyeonggi Province)

1614
01:02:40,668 --> 01:02:41,808
I need to go straight.

1615
01:02:41,808 --> 01:02:43,678
(Moved in on November 23, 1994)

1616
01:02:44,678 --> 01:02:46,478
I hope the apartment is still there.

1617
01:02:46,478 --> 01:02:47,848
I hoped the same thing.

1618
01:02:47,848 --> 01:02:49,578
- I think it'll be there. - I had expectations.

1619
01:02:49,878 --> 01:02:51,478
Yes. There was a shopping arcade.

1620
01:02:54,718 --> 01:02:58,688
(He passes the shopping arcade and enters the apartment complex.)

1621
01:03:00,588 --> 01:03:01,588
That's it.

1622
01:03:03,258 --> 01:03:05,858
That's right. There was a mountain.

1623
01:03:09,398 --> 01:03:11,938
(His memories become clearer.)

1624
01:03:12,968 --> 01:03:14,468
- The apartment your parents won. - Yes.

1625
01:03:15,508 --> 01:03:16,508
(Laughing)

1626
01:03:18,078 --> 01:03:21,048
(On which floor did I live?)

1627
01:03:22,348 --> 01:03:23,848
That was my place.

1628
01:03:23,848 --> 01:03:25,848
(That was my place.)

1629
01:03:26,348 --> 01:03:27,648
That was my place.

1630
01:03:27,648 --> 01:03:30,888
(He becomes tearful once again.)

1631
01:03:31,888 --> 01:03:33,428
- Why did his voice change? - Is he crying again?

1632
01:03:33,688 --> 01:03:34,758
Is he crying again?

1633
01:03:36,188 --> 01:03:37,228
It's a bit...

1634
01:03:37,358 --> 01:03:38,558
- I mean... - It's a bit too much.

1635
01:03:38,558 --> 01:03:39,658
- Seriously. - Listen.

1636
01:03:39,658 --> 01:03:40,728
- I'm sorry, - It's a bit...

1637
01:03:40,728 --> 01:03:42,198
- Kim Dae Ho. - but it isn't my memory.

1638
01:03:42,198 --> 01:03:43,438
Are you crying because you lost your house?

1639
01:03:43,438 --> 01:03:44,768
- No. - I mean...

1640
01:03:44,998 --> 01:03:46,398
- Why are you crying? - Seriously.

1641
01:03:46,398 --> 01:03:47,608
- Could it be... - Perhaps...

1642
01:03:47,608 --> 01:03:49,978
- He's so emotional. - we should change the perspective.

1643
01:03:49,978 --> 01:03:51,838
Are you crying because you sold it...

1644
01:03:51,838 --> 01:03:53,238
before the price rose?

1645
01:03:53,238 --> 01:03:56,048
You know, my parents worked themselves to the bone...

1646
01:03:56,048 --> 01:03:58,178
when they were younger than me...

1647
01:03:58,578 --> 01:04:00,488
- and bought that apartment. - You're a family man.

1648
01:04:00,488 --> 01:04:01,518
Yes.

1649
01:04:02,618 --> 01:04:05,458
(The memories of the past make him emotional.)

1650
01:04:07,188 --> 01:04:08,588
I didn't know that I was so sentimental.

1651
01:04:08,588 --> 01:04:10,098
- I get your reaction. - Yes.

1652
01:04:10,098 --> 01:04:11,458
- It's tear-jerking. - Yes.

1653
01:04:11,498 --> 01:04:13,628
- They worked hard to live there. - That's right.

1654
01:04:13,798 --> 01:04:16,998
He thought it'd be gone, but it was there.

1655
01:04:16,998 --> 01:04:18,568
He became very sentimental.

1656
01:04:19,198 --> 01:04:20,808
Also, I could see myself.

1657
01:04:20,808 --> 01:04:22,038
- When I was a child, - From childhood?

1658
01:04:22,038 --> 01:04:23,938
I went to school from there.

1659
01:04:24,978 --> 01:04:28,008
(Taking photos)

1660
01:04:30,448 --> 01:04:31,878
My dad worked so hard.

1661
01:04:32,048 --> 01:04:34,488
My dad was working at a textile company...

1662
01:04:34,488 --> 01:04:37,318
when he got into an accident.

1663
01:04:37,318 --> 01:04:39,318
He was very sick.

1664
01:04:40,158 --> 01:04:43,328
There were rollers for dying the fabric.

1665
01:04:43,498 --> 01:04:44,898
My dad was wearing work clothes.

1666
01:04:44,898 --> 01:04:46,928
His work clothes got caught in the rollers.

1667
01:04:46,928 --> 01:04:47,928
Oh, no.

1668
01:04:48,028 --> 01:04:49,298
- So... - It could've been lethal.

1669
01:04:49,298 --> 01:04:50,498
It was so dangerous.

1670
01:04:50,738 --> 01:04:54,168
Thankfully, his colleague turned off the rollers.

1671
01:04:54,408 --> 01:04:57,908
So he only cracked his ribs.

1672
01:04:58,438 --> 01:05:02,048
That accident could've cost him his life.

1673
01:05:02,048 --> 01:05:04,418
I think my dad realized it at that moment.

1674
01:05:04,418 --> 01:05:07,448
"While work is important,"

1675
01:05:08,818 --> 01:05:10,458
"what's the use of it if I can't remain healthy?"

1676
01:05:11,088 --> 01:05:14,558
My father's hometown is Yangpyeong.

1677
01:05:14,558 --> 01:05:16,058
All of family members live in Yangpyeong.

1678
01:05:16,488 --> 01:05:17,898
"I'll farm there..."

1679
01:05:18,098 --> 01:05:21,698
"and live without any greed." With that thought,

1680
01:05:21,698 --> 01:05:24,068
he decided to move there.

1681
01:05:24,498 --> 01:05:27,668
I still remember how much my parents struggled back then.

1682
01:05:29,108 --> 01:05:32,578
(On his way out after seeing the apartment of his memories)

1683
01:05:33,608 --> 01:05:35,908
(Trudging)

1684
01:05:40,018 --> 01:05:41,588
I think my mom sold the apartment...

1685
01:05:41,588 --> 01:05:43,118
through one of these real estate offices.

1686
01:05:46,018 --> 01:05:47,388
I should go and ask.

1687
01:05:48,458 --> 01:05:49,558
A real estate office?

1688
01:05:50,998 --> 01:05:52,958
Hello. I have a question.

1689
01:05:52,958 --> 01:05:54,668
Have you run this real estate office for many years?

1690
01:05:55,228 --> 01:05:57,338
(Nodding)

1691
01:05:57,998 --> 01:06:00,208
I remember how my mom sold the apartment...

1692
01:06:00,208 --> 01:06:01,508
through one of these real estate offices...

1693
01:06:01,908 --> 01:06:04,508
before moving elsewhere.

1694
01:06:05,308 --> 01:06:06,708
You don't keep those records, do you?

1695
01:06:07,048 --> 01:06:08,848
I do keep them.

1696
01:06:09,078 --> 01:06:10,648
Even the old ones?

1697
01:06:11,448 --> 01:06:14,748
I lived in...

1698
01:06:14,748 --> 01:06:17,088
- What? - It was fascinating.

1699
01:06:18,058 --> 01:06:20,128
All right. I was curious,

1700
01:06:20,128 --> 01:06:22,388
so I got a copy of the family register.

1701
01:06:22,888 --> 01:06:24,728
I wanted to see if you had the record.

1702
01:06:26,098 --> 01:06:27,698
You even have the very old records.

1703
01:06:28,368 --> 01:06:29,828
- Gosh, that's... - It's an old ledger.

1704
01:06:29,828 --> 01:06:31,338
It's handwritten.

1705
01:06:32,098 --> 01:06:33,908
- He has records from that time? - How cool.

1706
01:06:34,508 --> 01:06:39,038
We made a report on moving on November 17, 1994.

1707
01:06:39,038 --> 01:06:40,408
So it must've happened afterward.

1708
01:06:40,948 --> 01:06:42,708
These records are from 1994.

1709
01:06:42,708 --> 01:06:44,378
- I see. - Gosh, are they from 1994?

1710
01:06:44,378 --> 01:06:45,448
Here it is.

1711
01:06:45,878 --> 01:06:47,018
I was so surprised.

1712
01:06:47,018 --> 01:06:48,318
Here it is.

1713
01:06:49,018 --> 01:06:50,118
Kim Seok Geun.

1714
01:06:51,288 --> 01:06:53,258
It's 418-5357.

1715
01:06:54,228 --> 01:06:56,858
(Even after 30 years, his dad's name is on the ledger.)

1716
01:06:56,858 --> 01:06:59,198
I can't believe it.

1717
01:06:59,498 --> 01:07:01,568
That's my dad.

1718
01:07:02,298 --> 01:07:04,868
You really cherish your memories.

1719
01:07:06,538 --> 01:07:08,938
Back then, you...

1720
01:07:09,308 --> 01:07:11,178
You made a deal with my dad.

1721
01:07:11,178 --> 01:07:13,278
The real estate office wasn't here.

1722
01:07:13,278 --> 01:07:14,678
- It was over there. - That's right.

1723
01:07:14,778 --> 01:07:16,278
It was a long time ago.

1724
01:07:16,278 --> 01:07:17,748
My mom thought...

1725
01:07:18,178 --> 01:07:20,188
that her children would live in Seoul...

1726
01:07:20,188 --> 01:07:22,188
for their universities or such...

1727
01:07:22,188 --> 01:07:23,718
even after moving to Yangpyeong.

1728
01:07:23,718 --> 01:07:26,688
- So we held on to the apartment. - She held onto it until the end.

1729
01:07:26,928 --> 01:07:28,958
- It was her house. - But later on,

1730
01:07:28,958 --> 01:07:30,998
living in the countryside became difficult...

1731
01:07:30,998 --> 01:07:32,658
and they needed the money.

1732
01:07:32,658 --> 01:07:33,768
- So she sold it. - She sold it.

1733
01:07:33,768 --> 01:07:35,868
- She sold it after two years. - My goodness.

1734
01:07:36,198 --> 01:07:37,738
- Thank you. - Don't mention it.

1735
01:07:37,738 --> 01:07:39,138
- Thank you. - All right.

1736
01:07:39,138 --> 01:07:40,908
I asked just in case.

1737
01:07:41,068 --> 01:07:43,338
- Please stay healthy. - Okay.

1738
01:07:43,338 --> 01:07:45,038
- Thank you. - It was nice meeting you.

1739
01:07:45,038 --> 01:07:46,508
Thank you.

1740
01:07:47,008 --> 01:07:49,608
(He found a trace of his dad from 30 years ago.)

1741
01:07:50,818 --> 01:07:53,448
I didn't expect to see my dad's name there.

1742
01:07:55,848 --> 01:07:58,688
It really felt like I was traveling back in time.

1743
01:07:58,688 --> 01:08:00,828
- I can't believe there are records. - I got goosebumps.

1744
01:08:00,988 --> 01:08:02,528
- How fascinating. - It was fascinating indeed.

1745
01:08:03,728 --> 01:08:06,258
(He walks down the street as if he was traveling back in time.)

1746
01:08:06,628 --> 01:08:08,828
(Staring)

1747
01:08:08,828 --> 01:08:11,198
Back then, they were doing construction work here.

1748
01:08:13,708 --> 01:08:14,838
What?

1749
01:08:15,008 --> 01:08:18,438
Apartments popped up like they do in a new town.

1750
01:08:18,608 --> 01:08:20,138
- I see. - So an elementary school...

1751
01:08:20,138 --> 01:08:22,778
- was new as well. - That's right.

1752
01:08:22,778 --> 01:08:24,918
- That's right. - There were so many students...

1753
01:08:25,148 --> 01:08:26,848
that the classes were divided into the morning and afternoon ones.

1754
01:08:26,848 --> 01:08:28,888
- My goodness. - Really?

1755
01:08:28,888 --> 01:08:31,118
- There were so many kids back then. - Seriously.

1756
01:08:32,018 --> 01:08:33,188
That's right.

1757
01:08:33,728 --> 01:08:36,858
I think my classroom was on the second floor.

1758
01:08:37,758 --> 01:08:39,028
(It's another elementary school Dae Ho attended in 1995.)

1759
01:08:39,028 --> 01:08:40,228
That's right.

1760
01:08:42,398 --> 01:08:43,768
It really brings back memories.

1761
01:08:46,868 --> 01:08:48,008
Hello.

1762
01:08:48,168 --> 01:08:49,468
Thank you.

1763
01:08:49,468 --> 01:08:50,478
(Absorbed in memories, he gets into a taxi.)

1764
01:08:51,638 --> 01:08:53,438
Maybe that's a taxi you rode in the past.

1765
01:08:53,438 --> 01:08:54,448
No.

1766
01:08:54,448 --> 01:08:56,348
- That's an electric car. - "Sir, do you know me?"

1767
01:08:56,348 --> 01:08:58,248
- That's an electric car. - Then he'll hug the driver and cry.

1768
01:09:01,288 --> 01:09:02,818
(Sniffling)

1769
01:09:03,918 --> 01:09:04,988
Is he crying again?

1770
01:09:05,688 --> 01:09:07,488
(Staring)

1771
01:09:07,828 --> 01:09:09,228
How many more times will you cry from now on?

1772
01:09:10,958 --> 01:09:13,358
- I'm curious. - Knowing that will put me at ease.

1773
01:09:13,358 --> 01:09:14,828
(The crybaby, Dae Ho feels embarrassed.)

1774
01:09:17,738 --> 01:09:19,798
(His eyes turn teary again.)

1775
01:09:20,638 --> 01:09:24,208
(He heads over to a place with his teary eyes.)

1776
01:09:24,478 --> 01:09:27,648
I'm on my way to meet someone precious...

1777
01:09:27,648 --> 01:09:29,148
that I really missed.

1778
01:09:30,518 --> 01:09:33,478
Today, I'll visit my former teacher...

1779
01:09:33,918 --> 01:09:36,188
for the 1st time in 30 years.

1780
01:09:36,188 --> 01:09:39,318
After my family moved in an apartment, I attended...

1781
01:09:39,318 --> 01:09:40,688
Sigok Elementary School.

1782
01:09:41,228 --> 01:09:43,828
He taught me then.

1783
01:09:43,828 --> 01:09:44,958
- Really? - I see.

1784
01:09:44,958 --> 01:09:47,898
I've only known him for four months.

1785
01:09:47,898 --> 01:09:50,198
My dad got into an accident shortly after we moved there,

1786
01:09:50,198 --> 01:09:51,938
so we ended up going to Yangpyeong right away.

1787
01:09:52,238 --> 01:09:53,768
To my homeroom teacher of the new school,

1788
01:09:53,768 --> 01:09:55,808
he sent a letter.

1789
01:09:56,408 --> 01:09:58,438
- "He's like this as a student." - The duration isn't important.

1790
01:09:58,638 --> 01:09:59,908
I didn't know about it back then.

1791
01:10:00,238 --> 01:10:02,278
I only heard about it much later.

1792
01:10:02,578 --> 01:10:04,648
"There isn't a teacher like him. You should visit him sometime."

1793
01:10:04,648 --> 01:10:07,618
I've lived with that memory for over 30 years.

1794
01:10:08,188 --> 01:10:09,218
Yes. 30 years.

1795
01:10:09,218 --> 01:10:10,618
- He's a true teacher. - "I'll visit him some day."

1796
01:10:12,788 --> 01:10:15,958
(He's on his way to meet his teacher after 30 years.)

1797
01:10:19,098 --> 01:10:20,428
You look a bit nervous.

1798
01:10:20,598 --> 01:10:21,728
- A bit. - Right?

1799
01:10:21,728 --> 01:10:23,768
It was my 1st time seeing him after 30 years.

1800
01:10:23,768 --> 01:10:26,168
- Does he still work? - He still works.

1801
01:10:26,168 --> 01:10:27,368
- Really? - That's incredible.

1802
01:10:29,668 --> 01:10:31,108
- Is this my destination? - Yes.

1803
01:10:31,108 --> 01:10:32,208
Thank you.

1804
01:10:32,208 --> 01:10:33,678
- Thank you, sir. - All right.

1805
01:10:33,678 --> 01:10:35,978
Since he still worked as a teacher,

1806
01:10:35,978 --> 01:10:38,778
I went to see him around the time the school ended.

1807
01:10:40,318 --> 01:10:43,018
(Standing in front of his former teacher's school,)

1808
01:10:44,358 --> 01:10:45,488
He must be nervous.

1809
01:10:45,488 --> 01:10:47,228
(Dae Ho waits without a word.)

1810
01:10:47,888 --> 01:10:49,488
You're handsome.

1811
01:10:49,488 --> 01:10:50,658
(Smiling)

1812
